[38;5;231m[49m⏺[39m [1mSection 2: error handling and UI wiring.[0m

  [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m fails in more ways than it looks. Safari private mode throws [38;5;153mQuotaExceededError[39m on every write; a user
  can disable site data entirely so [38;5;153mwindow.localStorage[39m access itself throws a [38;5;153mSecurityError[39m; and stored JSON can be
  corrupt because anything on the page — or the user via devtools — can overwrite the key.

  So the module never throws and never assumes:

  - Availability is probed once on load (write/read/delete a throwaway key inside [38;5;153mtry[39m). If unavailable, the module falls
    back to an in-memory object. The page keeps working, preferences just don't survive the tab.
  - [38;5;153mget()[39m wraps the parse. Malformed JSON, or a stored value that isn't an object, is treated as "no preferences" and
    the entry is reset rather than left to throw on every subsequent read.
  - [38;5;153mset()[39m returns [38;5;153mfalse[39m on a quota or security failure instead of throwing, so a caller can react. No silent [38;5;153mcatch {}[39m.

  UI wiring in [38;5;153mindex.html[39m and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m:

  - A [38;5;153m<label><input type="checkbox" id="remember-username"> Remember me</label>[39m added to the form.
  - On submit, [1mafter[0m validation passes: if checked, [38;5;153mPrefs.set('username', username)[39m; if unchecked,
    [38;5;153mPrefs.remove('username')[39m — so unticking actively clears a previously stored value rather than leaving it behind.
  - On page load, read the stored username; if present, pre-fill [38;5;153m#username[39m and tick the checkbox.
  - The password is never read, written, or referenced by [38;5;153mprefs.js[39m. Storing it is out of scope here and I wouldn't add
    it later without a separate conversation.

  Two deliberate omissions: no expiry on the stored username (localStorage has no TTL, and hand-rolling one for a
  "remember me" field is complexity without a requirement), and no cross-tab [38;5;153mstorage[39m event sync (the value is only read
  at load).

  Does the error handling and wiring look right? Testing is the last section.

